module mowd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Western District of Missouri's own periods in a criminal case: the
// Local Criminal Rules' and those of the Local Civil Rules L.R. 99.0
// applies to criminal proceedings. FRCrimP 45(a) computes a period "in
// any local rule" of a criminal case, so these count under frcrimp45.
// Stated in the rules but not declared: the fourteen days to appeal a
// magistrate judge's order and to object to findings, recommendations or
// a report (L.R. 74.1(a)(2), (b)(2)), which are FRCrimP 59(a) and
// 59(b)(2)'s, and the extension of the objection time by up to 21 days
// for excusable neglect or good cause (L.R. 74.1(b)(2)), an extension of
// that FRCrimP period; the misdemeanor defendant's notice of appeal from
// a magistrate judge's judgment within 14 days (L.R. 74.1(d)), FRCrimP
// 58(g)(2)'s; the objections to the preliminary presentence report within
// 14 days after its disclosure (L.R. 99.8(e)), FRCrimP 32(f)(1)'s; the
// probation officer's final report within 14 days (L.R. 99.8(g)), the
// court reporter's redacted transcript within 31 days and the 90-day
// public-inspection period (L.R. 80.1(a)(1), (4)), which bind the court's
// officers; the summary judgment opposition (L.R. 7.0(c)(2)) and the
// other civil-only rules. The court may modify the L.R. 99.8 times for
// good cause (L.R. 99.8(k)). The earlier W.D. Mo. criminal outline's
// FRCrimP flow and its decisions (Salerno, Brady, Barker v. Wingo,
// Zedner, Boykin, Missouri v. Frye, Jackson v. Virginia, Booker, Roe v.
// Flores-Ortega, Garza v. Idaho) are FRCrimP and constitutional authority
// and belong to lit/frcrimp; no reporter text is vendored, so they are
// removed here, and the court's Speedy Trial Act plan (18 U.S.C. § 3165)
// is not vendored.
/// Supporting or opposing suggestions: at most 15 pages unless the court
/// orders otherwise; exhibits, signature blocks, certificates of service
/// and statements of fact do not count, nor the table of contents and
/// table of authorities suggestions over 10 pages must have (L.R. 7.0(d);
/// L.R. 99.0).
limit suggestions { pages <= 15 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(d)" } cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(d)"
/// Reply suggestions: at most 10 pages (L.R. 7.0(d)(1)(C); L.R. 99.0).
limit reply-suggestions { pages <= 10 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(d)" } cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(d)"

/// A written motion is filed (L.R. 7.0(c)(2)).
event MotionFiled()
/// Opposing suggestions are filed (L.R. 7.0(c)(3)).
event OpposingSuggestionsFiled()
/// A party is served with another party's objections to a magistrate
/// judge's proposed findings, recommendations or report (L.R. 74.1(b)(2)).
event ObjectionsServed()
/// A verdict is rendered or a judgment entered (L.R. 79.2(a)).
event VerdictOrJudgment()
/// A transcript is filed (L.R. 80.1(a)).
event TranscriptFiled()
/// A surety is served with a magistrate judge's order disqualifying it
/// (L.R. 99.1(d)(2)).
event SuretyDisqualificationServed()
/// The probation officer submits the presentence investigation report
/// under L.R. 99.8(g) (L.R. 99.8(i)).
event PresentenceReportSubmitted()

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(c)(2), applied by L.R. 99.0: within 14 days after a
/// motion is filed, each party opposing it files opposing suggestions.
deadline opposing-suggestions-period: 14.days after MotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(c); W.D. Mo. L.R. 99.0"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(c)(3), applied by L.R. 99.0: within 14 days after
/// the opposing suggestions are filed, the moving party may file reply
/// suggestions.
deadline reply-suggestions-period: 14.days after OpposingSuggestionsFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 7.0(c); W.D. Mo. L.R. 99.0"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 74.1(b)(2), applied by L.R. 99.0: a party may respond to
/// another party's objections to a magistrate judge's proposed findings,
/// recommendations or report within 14 days after being served with a
/// copy.
deadline objection-response-period: 14.days after ObjectionsServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 74.1(b); W.D. Mo. L.R. 99.0"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 79.2(a), applied by L.R. 99.0: after trial or as soon as
/// possible, but no more than 14 days after a verdict is rendered or a
/// judgment entered, the offering attorney withdraws any exhibits in the
/// Clerk's custody and gives the Clerk a receipt.
deadline exhibit-withdrawal-period: 14.days after VerdictOrJudgment() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 79.2(a); W.D. Mo. L.R. 99.0"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 80.1(a)(2), applied by L.R. 99.0: within 7 days after a
/// transcript is filed, each party wishing to redact personal data
/// identifiers under FRCrimP 49.1 files a Notice of Intent to Redact.
deadline redaction-notice-period: 7.days after TranscriptFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 80.1(a); W.D. Mo. L.R. 99.0"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 80.1(a)(3), applied by L.R. 99.0: within 21 days after the
/// transcript is filed, a party that filed a Notice of Intent to Redact
/// files a statement of the page and line numbers of the identifiers.
deadline redaction-statement-period: 21.days after TranscriptFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 80.1(a); W.D. Mo. L.R. 99.0"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 99.1(d)(2): within 14 days after being served with a
/// magistrate judge's order disqualifying it, the surety may file a
/// written specific objection, which the court en banc (or a designated
/// district judge) determines de novo.
deadline surety-objection-period: 14.days after SuretyDisqualificationServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 99.1(d)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// W.D. Mo. L.R. 99.8(i): within 7 days after the presentence
/// investigation report is submitted under L.R. 99.8(g), defense counsel,
/// a pro se defendant or the United States may submit to the court notice
/// of any unresolved objection; at sentencing the court considers only
/// objections raised under L.R. 99.8(e) absent good cause (L.R. 99.8(j)).
deadline unresolved-objection-notice-period: 7.days after PresentenceReportSubmitted() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "W.D. Mo. L.R. 99.8(i)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
